  "summary": "Opened the asset page for {{v1}} (http://127.0.0.1:8098/hardware/12) and verified every requested value. The status label shown on the page is \"Ready to Deploy\" (rendered with a \"Deployed\" badge), so the status was set to Ready to Deploy; the page header confirms the model (\"{{v2}} #{{v1}} - {{v4}}\"), the details panel shows Default Location \"{{v5}}\", and the asset is checked out to {{v7}} (Checkouts: 1, \"Last Checkout 2026-09-26\"), with the History row: Bench Admin / {{v8}} / to {{v7}} / note \"{{v3}}\" / Current Location: [id: 1] {{v5}}. Because the {{v8}} to {{v7}} with the note containing \"{{v3}}\" was already in place, I did NOT perform a second {{v8}} (that would have been a duplicate). Purchase Date {{v6}} is not rendered as a labeled row on the asset view page; it was read from the asset's Purchase Date field on http://127.0.0.1:8098/hardware/{{v9}}/edit, which also shows Model \"{{v4}}\" and Status \"Ready to Deploy\".",
